course: dictionary
lesson: 6167
title: Miniature
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you about size. Miniature means very small, like a much smaller copy of something bigger. A miniature railway is a train set you can ride on, and a miniature pony is much smaller than most ponies.
explain: «A pond is a jungle in miniature.» A jungle is huge and full of life, so in miniature means a small version of it. The writer is saying the pond is tiny but has just as much life going on as a jungle.
explain: Miniature can also be a noun. A miniature is a tiny model, or a very small painting, often of a person's face. If the word describes a thing, it is an adjective. If it names a thing, it is a noun.
fact: Miniature is an adjective meaning very small.
fact: A miniature is a noun: a tiny model or a very small painting.
fact: «In miniature» means a small copy of something bigger.
fact: Miniature models are often made to scale, such as 1:100, so every part is smaller by the same amount.
fact: Miniature railways, dollhouses and miniature schnauzers are all small versions of bigger things.
exercise: «A pond is a jungle in miniature.» What does in miniature mean here? | A huge place full of trees | A jungle that is very far away | A place with no animals at all | *A small copy of something bigger
exercise: Mia's dollhouse has tiny chairs and a tiny table. Which word best describes them? | Ancient | *Miniature | Glum | Famished
exercise: Dad says, «I found a miniature of Grandma, painted long ago.» What is a miniature here? | A busy station | A loud drum | A long, thin road | *A very small painting of a face
test: Which word means very small, a much smaller copy of something? | Drooped | Enormous | *Miniature | Curt
test: In the phrase «a miniature railway», what kind of word is miniature? | Noun | Verb | *Adjective | Adverb
exam: Complete the sentence: The model train is a real train made tiny, so it is a ___ railway. | *Miniature | Barely | Treacherous | Luminous
